<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William IV, Prince of Orange</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1711">1711</a>–1751</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William IV, Prince of Orange, was a prince of the Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Dietz</a> line who inherited the Orange claims and gathered all the lands of the Nassau-Ottonian branch by 1743. During the French invasion of 1747 he was made hereditary stadtholder of all the provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. His descendants became the kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-iv-prince-of-orange.jpg" alt="William IV, Prince of Orange" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Aved · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Willem_IV_(1711-1751),_prins_van_Oranje-Nassau,_SK-A-880.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
